 "about": "Consumer admission per capability group (OUT1.n). A group is visible to a consumer only when its admission record satisfies door.admission_gaps for the running revision and host; no record means hidden. tier MAINTAINER and PARK are never visible. Records are written only from an installed end to end run and an independent rating, never by hand from a source tree. Door capability patterns end in * to match a prefix. CORE groups (the product's own path) are admitted on installed journey rows named in journey_rows and walked by scripts/journey/run_journey.py; every other tier needs the full record door.admission_gaps checks. supported_hosts lists only hosts a journey was walked on. A journey row that is not PASS on the walked revision is never cited.",
